E. Proof pull
  The old phase-color exactness is useful here, but the continuous mass
  does not see the AP84 mod-35 component clock: E={0} kills color 0 and
  leaves thirteen identical live layers.  The AP-tail coloring signal is
  the shifted grid and boundary sidecar.  HYP-3456's period-35 escape
  clock remains a component/corridor count; HYP-3459 records the legal
  AP84 color-packet quotient, HYP-3460 records the phase-branch
  pullback, and HYP-3461 records the colored-extension carrier,
  with HYP-3458 retaining the
  35-state coloring-recursion packet.  HYP-3470 supplies the exact q=14V
  color-grid placement clock that should be carried if the AP-tail splice
  uses CRT witnesses rather than branch-union components.
  Next theorem target: prove the fixed four-interval color-grid formula
  symbolically and attach its period-385/5005 sidecar to the HYP-3439
  AP-tail descent only when actual q=14V witness placement is needed.

